00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:06.940 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  welcome to noob gaming Network in this  video I'll show how to complete time  square power relay on legendary  difficulty solo I'm doing this on  console with a standard controller and  I've particularly average aim on a good  day if you follow what I do here I  believe anyone regardless of skill  should be able to complete this mission  of the three legendary missions this one  is the easiest attention needs to be put  more into remembering where and win the  NPC spawn so rather than having to be  reactive it's more about being prepared  before we start you want to be using a  skill power build and a sniper here I'm  using a high skill power fire Chryst and  technicians build I'll leave a link in  the description I've broken this mission  down into four parts  number one the beginning number two  stairway to street number three balcony  waves number four boss fight  for this first part you want to have the  fire turret and cluster seeker mine  equipped the top of these stairs is  where you going to hold as the first few  waves will push towards you place your  turret somewhere on the handrails to  slow down the rushes  if you're feeling a bit pushed don't  hesitate and running outside to take  some cover and re-establish your defense  use your si combines to help find any  hidden enemies and clear out the  remainder of the NPCs  [Music]  when you're satisfied that there isn't  any more coming head down the stairs to  the left there's usually a couple of  snipers use your sniper or secant lines  to clear the matter  for the end of this part you can head  towards a room on the left where you're  being directed to turn off the power  before you run and hang back a bit  there'll be a shielded heavy that will  need to be taken out first  [Music]  once the power has been turned off you  can head towards the stairway that'll  take you up to the street  much like the first part you'll be  setting up the defensive position on  these steers as a few waves of enemies  will be rushing towards you use your  turret to slow them and your seekers to  hunt them down  occasionally you'll need to trigger off  the next wave by running up towards the  top of the stairs just keep an eye on  your mini-map as often you'll think  they're cleared but there'll be one guy  just hiding out stopping Nick's wave  from spawning as long as you're prepared  you can just fall back and have your  skills do the work  once the waves are cleared head to the  top of the stairs and take out four  single sniper on the left after that run  towards the balcony further down the  road to the right  ignoring the NPC's in the middle of the  street weren't straight up the stairs  this balcony is where you'll be spending  a large amount of time for the rest of  the mission so get comfy this part can  take a while but patience and  understanding when the NPCs will spawn  is the key  after the first couple of waves you'll  be tasked with taking this case towards  the end of the street you need to  transport this bit by bit keeping a  close eye on your mini-map as soon as  you see enemies appear drop it and  sprint back to the balcony about now  you'll want to change out your flame  turret for a healing station some of the  enemies will now start firing sticky  bombs and seeker mines at you with the  right shot they'll drop you on one hurt  so you want the station to keep you heal  up and revive you if necessary in this  example I've changed to a reclaim build  to get the best out of the healing  station keep inching the case closer to  the fuse box at the end of the street  once this is done you'll have another  wave of enemies this time with a few  snipers  you can either snipe them back or move a  little closer to have your secret mines  take them out  once you've taken out the first two  you'll need to move further down the  road to deal with the remaining two at  the back  after they did run back to the balcony  and take care of the last wave of  enemies before the boss wave  you'll know when X the boss wave because  you'll see a number of purple NPCs  hovering just out of range down the  street  this part isn't actually too hard once  you know what you're doing there will be  two bosses a sniper and a heavy and a  bunch of purpose sitting out of range  you can easily take out the Purple's and  the sniper boss first  don't even bother shooting it the heavy  for now just leave them until the end  the only way you can take down this boss  is to shoot the redhead Fox on his back  the trouble is is quite hard to get him  to turn around when you're playing solo  the easiest way I find is to change over  to ear bursts Iike mines and keep  setting them on fire the flame turret  works too but he'll keep running out of  range  [Music]  if you keep doing this and chipping away  at his hitbox he should drop pretty  quick in this example I was having an  absolute nightmare my aim just wasn't on  point  if you found this useful and you'd like  me to release a video on the other two  legendary missions let me know in the  comments below otherwise thanks for  watching and I'd like to take this  opportunity to thank everyone for the  amazing feedback I've been receiving  lately it means a lot at the end of the  day this is just a hobby for me but it's  really awesome to see that others are  appreciating and finding the stuff  useful so thank you again and see you in  the next video  [Music]

